{
 "id": "camera_catchup",
 "label": "Camera Catches Up",
 "category": "Time",
 "tags": ["look"],
 "version": 1,
 "blurb": "Makes the picture behave like a camera whose auto exposure and white balance are always a moment behind. Walk out of a dark room and the frame blows out to white, then pulls down, overshoots a little and settles; the lights go off and it sinks into black before it lifts again. Cut from a warm room to a blue street and the street comes in too blue and slowly turns neutral. It reacts to whatever the light in the footage does, cuts and flashes included, with no keyframes.",
 "history": {"max": 62, "reach": ["settle", 2.6], "seconds": ["settle"]},
